{"id":"chatcmpl-7caddc26-7599-497f-96c3-8059a6a6a591","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250355,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: when a visual question requires distinguishing between similar findings (e.g., left vs. right laterality), query multiple independent vision-language models with targeted, descriptive prompts and require agreement before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any ambiguous classification task where a single model's output may be unreliable and where spatial/locational reasoning is the discriminating factor.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When two answer options differ only by a spatial attribute (laterality, location, orientation), explicitly ask the model to describe the location and appearance of the finding rather than just classify it.\",\n    \"Use two or more independent expert models/tools to answer the same diagnostic question, and treat concordance as evidence and discordance as a signal to gather more information.\",\n    \"Frame tool queries to elicit descriptive evidence (location, appearance, volume loss) that directly supports or refutes each candidate option, rather than asking for a bare label.\",\n    \"Reserve the final answer for after cross-validation, citing the agreement of independent sources as the justification.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Query specialized vision models with prompts that ask for anatomical location and descriptive features, not just the diagnosis label; require agreement across at least two independent models before answering.\",\n    \"Ambiguous multiple-choice classification\": \"Identify the single attribute that distinguishes the options (e.g., laterality) and design queries that force the model to report that attribute explicitly.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification\": \"Use heterogeneous tools (different model families) so their errors are less likely to correlate; concordance across independent tools is stronger evidence than repeated queries to one tool.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm that at least two independent models/tools agree on the discriminating attribute (e.g., laterality) before finalizing the answer.\",\n    \"Verify that each tool's response explicitly addresses the distinguishing feature between the candidate options, not just a generic diagnosis.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":517,"total_tokens":935,"completion_tokens":418,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":517},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":418}}}